WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:54.730
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:55.000 --> 00:58.020
"Not Yours"

3
00:58.100 --> 01:00.800
(Episode 7)

4
01:10.200 --> 01:11.920
Your bed is so comfortable.

5
01:12.000 --> 01:13.999
I'm staying at your place tonight.

6
01:14.079 --> 01:15.640
I'll just crash here, okay?

7
01:29.640 --> 01:30.880
You haven't even been drinking.

8
01:31.519 --> 01:32.519
Why are you blushing?

9
01:36.519 --> 01:37.519
You did this to me.

10
01:39.239 --> 01:40.840
When did I do anything to you?

11
01:40.920 --> 01:42.599
You're the one messing with me, okay?

12
01:51.159 --> 01:52.560
Let me ask you something.

13
01:52.640 --> 01:54.920
Does what you said last time still count?

14
01:57.239 --> 01:58.600
Huh? What was it?

15
01:58.680 --> 02:00.239
You said if I won the lottery,

16
02:00.319 --> 02:01.719
you'd be my assistant.

17
02:04.239 --> 02:05.519
Yeah, I did.

18
02:06.319 --> 02:08.120
I, Jiang Weibang, am a man of my word.

19
02:10.560 --> 02:11.759
No way, did you actually win?

20
02:19.800 --> 02:20.800
See for yourself.

21
02:21.639 --> 02:22.639
No way!

22
02:22.680 --> 02:24.440
Damn, you really won!

23
02:24.520 --> 02:25.119
What prize did you get?

24
02:25.199 --> 02:26.199
How much?

25
02:27.840 --> 02:29.240
That's beside the point.

26
02:30.639 --> 02:32.040
The point is, are you in or not?

27
02:32.120 --> 02:33.639
How is that beside the point?

28
02:33.719 --> 02:34.719
How much?

29
02:39.719 --> 02:41.159
If you take the job,

30
02:42.120 --> 02:43.840
I'll split half of it with you.

31
02:46.280 --> 02:47.119
Half?

32
02:47.199 --> 02:48.079
Yeah.

33
02:48.159 --> 02:49.799
Then of course I'm in,

34
02:49.879 --> 02:50.879
Boss Li.

35
02:52.680 --> 02:55.359
Are you doing this for me, or for the money?

36
02:55.439 --> 02:56.919
For the money, obviously!

37
03:01.280 --> 03:02.295
I didn't even get a good look.

38
03:02.319 --> 03:03.160
You...

39
03:03.240 --> 03:04.240
Classic you.

40
03:06.960 --> 03:08.160
You can come work for me,

41
03:08.240 --> 03:10.120
but you need to tone down that temper of yours.

42
03:12.360 --> 03:14.439
Tone down my temper?

43
03:14.960 --> 03:17.280
I'm not saying you have a bad temper,

44
03:17.360 --> 03:19.895
it's just that you always pick a fight with Boss P'Eng whenever you meet.

45
03:19.919 --> 03:21.400
He's my future boss.

46
03:22.039 --> 03:23.719
It won't look good if you keep doing that.

47
03:24.759 --> 03:26.999
Well, he's the one who keeps provoking me for no reason.

48
03:27.400 --> 03:28.840
Can't you just do it for me?

49
03:31.319 --> 03:32.319
And for the money?

50
03:33.400 --> 03:34.439
Just hold back a little.

51
03:37.639 --> 03:39.160
So what you're saying is,

52
03:39.240 --> 03:41.679
you want me to be like you

53
03:41.759 --> 03:42.840
and be a total pushover?

54
03:45.560 --> 03:46.560
Me?

55
03:47.599 --> 03:48.639
A pushover?

56
03:50.800 --> 03:52.559
I refuse to be a pushover.

57
03:52.639 --> 03:53.879
It's way too exhausting.

58
03:55.360 --> 03:57.599
Everyday folks at the bottom like us

59
03:58.319 --> 04:00.479
have to be willing to push back and flip the table

60
04:01.000 --> 04:02.560
so people don't walk all over us.

61
04:03.120 --> 04:05.880
If he doesn't even respect me

62
04:05.960 --> 04:07.400
or care about my feelings,

63
04:08.039 --> 04:09.639
why on earth should I care about his?

64
04:12.560 --> 04:14.039
But have you ever thought that

65
04:14.919 --> 04:16.959
by always going head-to-head with people like this,

66
04:17.319 --> 04:18.680
you might end up losing a lot?

67
04:21.639 --> 04:23.240
I'm not afraid of losing anything.

68
04:24.439 --> 04:27.119
Even a best friend I used to spend every single day with

69
04:27.199 --> 04:28.839
could just up and leave without a word.

70
04:29.360 --> 04:31.120
You're the one who taught me that, Milan.

71
04:34.759 --> 04:36.199
Still, I have to thank you

72
04:37.120 --> 04:38.319
for making me realize

73
04:38.399 --> 04:40.199
that the only person I can rely on is myself.

74
04:42.279 --> 04:44.240
I didn't have a choice back then.

75
04:44.879 --> 04:46.080
When I became a trainee,

76
04:46.160 --> 04:48.016
the agency forbade me from contacting anyone privately

77
04:48.040 --> 04:49.679
and deleted all my contacts.

78
04:49.759 --> 04:50.439
There was nothing I could do.

79
04:50.519 --> 04:51.519
Alright,

80
04:52.120 --> 04:53.160
let's drop it.

81
04:53.240 --> 04:54.240
It's all in the past.

82
05:06.040 --> 05:07.040
Don't worry,

83
05:08.279 --> 05:09.720
I'll be your assistant.

84
05:10.879 --> 05:12.160
After all,

85
05:12.240 --> 05:13.960
it's not like I have another job right now.

86
05:32.319 --> 05:33.959
Why are you so nice to Pao Bei?

87
05:38.360 --> 05:39.399
Because he's worth it.

88
06:18.920 --> 06:20.120
What are you doing?

89
06:21.160 --> 06:21.960
What?

90
06:22.040 --> 06:23.160
Do you still not trust me?

91
06:24.480 --> 06:26.240
Tell me what you're up to first.

92
06:37.120 --> 06:38.120
Put this on first,

93
06:38.680 --> 06:41.040
and I'll take you to the place you're really curious about.

94
06:41.759 --> 06:43.120
Don't try anything funny.

95
06:43.639 --> 06:45.199
The kids are still downstairs.

96
06:45.279 --> 06:46.576
I had Mingkun take care of everything.

97
06:46.600 --> 06:47.600
Stop worrying.

98
07:09.279 --> 07:10.279
Where are we?

99
07:12.199 --> 07:14.159
Haven't you always been curious about this place?

100
07:14.560 --> 07:16.519
You even stole the key just to sneak in.

101
07:19.319 --> 07:22.160
So this is that mysterious room.

102
07:24.800 --> 07:26.400
Well, you made it so secretive,

103
07:26.480 --> 07:27.536
it naturally makes people want to know

104
07:27.560 --> 07:28.760
what actually goes on in here.

105
07:28.800 --> 07:30.000
So,

106
07:31.759 --> 07:33.799
were you afraid of people finding out

107
07:33.879 --> 07:35.720
because you wanted to hide your girly side?

108
07:36.560 --> 07:37.720
Girly side?

109
07:45.480 --> 07:46.800
More like childlike innocence.

110
08:01.959 --> 08:03.519
All of these

111
08:04.079 --> 08:07.279
are gifts my mom gave me before she passed away.

112
08:22.120 --> 08:23.240
I had no idea

113
08:24.000 --> 08:25.959
he had such a quiet and gentle side.

114
08:29.360 --> 08:30.360
Can I...

115
08:31.680 --> 08:33.200
Can I ask you a question?

116
08:33.919 --> 08:34.919
Go ahead.

117
08:37.879 --> 08:39.879
When did your mom...

118
08:40.559 --> 08:42.080
When did she pass away?

119
08:47.840 --> 08:48.840
Probably...

120
08:50.919 --> 08:52.720
Probably when I was around Xiaotong's age.

121
08:54.440 --> 08:56.080
You must miss her a lot.

122
09:05.360 --> 09:07.640
Don't look at me with that pitying expression.

123
09:07.720 --> 09:08.720
OK?

124
09:11.039 --> 09:12.200
I'm filthy rich.

125
09:14.960 --> 09:16.176
You should worry about yourself instead.

126
09:16.200 --> 09:17.200
Okay.

127
09:19.039 --> 09:20.199
By the way,

128
09:20.279 --> 09:21.816
there are snacks and drinks over there.

129
09:21.840 --> 09:22.880
Want to go check them out?

130
09:24.559 --> 09:26.320
Give my stomach a break.

131
09:27.759 --> 09:29.279
I'm seriously stuffed.

132
09:55.080 --> 09:56.240
Actually,

133
09:58.120 --> 09:59.639
before I met you,

134
10:01.159 --> 10:02.200
I felt like I was

135
10:03.159 --> 10:05.440
just a heartless money-making machine.

136
10:06.960 --> 10:08.760
But after meeting you,

137
10:08.840 --> 10:09.919
it suddenly hit me—

138
10:10.919 --> 10:11.919
wow,

139
10:12.960 --> 10:14.799
my life can actually be this exciting.

140
10:16.440 --> 10:18.120
Someone actually dares to talk back to me,

141
10:18.759 --> 10:20.159
and even fight with me.

142
10:21.559 --> 10:22.559
Do you have any idea

143
10:23.120 --> 10:24.279
how much that makes me

144
10:27.879 --> 10:30.399
feel like an actual human being?

145
10:34.279 --> 10:35.279
Today,

146
10:36.360 --> 10:37.879
hanging out with you guys all day

147
10:38.879 --> 10:40.720
and having a home-cooked meal together...

148
10:43.519 --> 10:44.679
I was genuinely happy.

149
10:47.120 --> 10:49.120
Happy from the bottom of my heart.

150
10:50.679 --> 10:51.840
So,

151
10:53.320 --> 10:55.360
you kept thanking me today,

152
10:56.600 --> 10:57.600
but really,

153
10:59.200 --> 11:00.720
the one who should be saying thank you

154
11:02.879 --> 11:03.919
is me.

155
11:09.759 --> 11:10.759
What's so funny?

156
11:11.440 --> 11:14.080
I rarely open up like this, okay?

157
11:14.879 --> 11:16.159
Could you show a little respect?

158
11:22.039 --> 11:23.160
It's just that hearing you

159
11:23.240 --> 11:24.800
suddenly talk like a normal human being

160
11:25.399 --> 11:27.919
is a little hard to get used to.

161
11:29.519 --> 11:30.519
A normal human being?

162
11:31.919 --> 11:32.919
Are you insulting me?

163
11:33.600 --> 11:34.880
Then what was I speaking before?

164
11:35.480 --> 11:36.480
Gibberish?

165
11:38.159 --> 11:39.360
Not at all!

166
11:39.440 --> 11:41.480
Talking like a human just means saying things

167
11:42.000 --> 11:43.120
that make people feel

168
11:45.279 --> 11:46.879
strangely sympathetic

169
11:49.440 --> 11:51.000
and weirdly touched.

170
11:52.679 --> 11:55.799
In my book, that's called "human talk" for short.

171
11:56.360 --> 11:59.679
Does that make sense to you?

172
12:02.799 --> 12:04.919
Stop being so sensitive, okay?

173
12:06.840 --> 12:07.919
Sensitive?

174
12:09.399 --> 12:11.440
I think you're the sensitive one here.

175
12:12.000 --> 12:12.679
Me?

176
12:12.759 --> 12:14.000
How am I sensitive?

177
12:14.879 --> 12:16.159
I am not sensitive at all, okay?

178
12:19.600 --> 12:20.720
Not sensitive, huh?

179
12:24.200 --> 12:25.480
Really not sensitive?

180
12:26.360 --> 12:27.360
What are you doing?

181
12:29.480 --> 12:30.720
Stop it, that tickles!

182
12:58.240 --> 12:59.840
Can I ask you a question?

183
13:01.840 --> 13:03.199
Yeah.

184
13:03.279 --> 13:04.279
Go ahead.

185
13:06.399 --> 13:07.399
Do you...

186
13:09.960 --> 13:11.200
Do you like me?

187
13:18.320 --> 13:19.559
Well, do you hate me?

188
13:22.120 --> 13:23.399
Of course I don't hate you.

189
13:24.639 --> 13:25.759
Then that means you like me,

190
13:26.240 --> 13:27.240
right?

191
13:38.799 --> 13:39.799
I'm a little thirsty.

192
13:39.879 --> 13:40.919
I'm gonna go grab a drink.

193
14:03.039 --> 14:04.480
Don't dodge my question.

194
14:06.840 --> 14:08.439
You do like me,

195
14:08.519 --> 14:09.519
don't you?

196
14:17.039 --> 14:18.480
I know you like me.

197
14:20.320 --> 14:21.679
Look how red your ears are.

198
14:23.240 --> 14:24.480
Let me cool them down for you.

199
14:29.360 --> 14:30.440
What are you doing?

200
14:34.720 --> 14:36.320
And you said you weren't sensitive.

201
14:37.399 --> 14:39.479
Just this much and you're already weak in the knees.

202
14:40.840 --> 14:41.840
So cute.

203
16:08.000 --> 16:09.360
Even if you don't say it,

204
16:11.039 --> 16:12.039
your actions

205
16:12.799 --> 16:14.320
speak louder than words.

206
16:18.159 --> 16:19.320
I like you.

207
16:23.080 --> 16:24.960
But I don't think we're right for each other.

208
16:34.399 --> 16:35.879
Why aren't we right for each other?

209
16:36.440 --> 16:38.319
I'm not done talking yet.

210
16:38.399 --> 16:39.440
I just...

211
16:49.000 --> 16:50.520
I'm not done yet.

212
16:50.600 --> 16:51.639
I just...

213
16:56.320 --> 16:57.600
I know what's holding you back.

214
16:59.039 --> 17:00.480
But I don't care about any of that.

215
17:02.240 --> 17:03.319
All I care about

216
17:03.399 --> 17:04.839
is how I feel about you right now.

217
17:09.720 --> 17:10.839
I want you.

218
17:13.000 --> 17:14.279
I want to be with you.

219
17:17.519 --> 17:18.519
Right here,

220
17:19.559 --> 17:20.680
there is no boss,

221
17:21.759 --> 17:22.799
and no debtor.

222
17:25.440 --> 17:26.680
There are just two men here,

223
17:28.440 --> 17:30.279
named Pao Bei

224
17:32.200 --> 17:34.359
and P'Eng.

225
17:39.960 --> 17:41.359
Two people who love each other.

226
17:43.880 --> 17:44.920
And that's enough.

227
17:52.640 --> 17:53.640
Then,

228
17:56.559 --> 17:58.279
please let me be yours tonight.

229
21:13.880 --> 21:14.880
Thank you.

230
21:35.319 --> 21:38.680
"Thank you for giving me a warm winter."

231
21:42.799 --> 21:44.519
This was sent from abroad.

232
21:45.240 --> 21:46.320
Yeah.

233
21:46.400 --> 21:47.400
From Norway.

234
21:53.480 --> 21:54.480
Well, well.

235
21:54.519 --> 21:56.559
Boss P'Eng even has romantic flings abroad.

236
22:11.720 --> 22:13.240
That's right.

237
22:14.359 --> 22:16.479
With your Boss P'Eng's looks

238
22:16.559 --> 22:17.800
and charm,

239
22:17.880 --> 22:19.360
he's bound to be a hit

240
22:19.440 --> 22:20.999
wherever he goes.

241
22:21.079 --> 22:22.079
Oh, really?

242
22:34.160 --> 22:35.519
What are you doing?

243
22:50.400 --> 22:51.560
Take a look.

244
22:51.640 --> 22:53.200
Isn't the handwriting the same?

245
23:01.480 --> 23:03.239
What do you mean?

246
23:03.319 --> 23:05.039
You wrote this yourself?

247
23:06.359 --> 23:07.239
Yeah.

248
23:07.319 --> 23:08.600
Silly boy.

249
23:08.680 --> 23:09.880
I sent it to myself.

250
23:10.440 --> 23:11.440
Get it now?

251
23:13.279 --> 23:15.160
So, the picture on this...

252
23:15.240 --> 23:16.599
The snowy mountains are gorgeous.

253
23:53.400 --> 23:54.400
Have you ever seen snow?

254
23:55.759 --> 23:56.759
No.

255
23:57.519 --> 23:59.319
It never snows here in Mancheng.

256
24:00.039 --> 24:01.640
I probably

257
24:01.720 --> 24:04.319
won't ever get the chance to see snow in my life.

258
24:06.599 --> 24:09.079
Norway was where I saw snow for the first time, too.

259
24:11.079 --> 24:12.400
The snow there has a kind of...

260
24:13.480 --> 24:14.880
How do I put it?

261
24:14.960 --> 24:17.640
It smells like Super Cedar.

262
24:17.720 --> 24:18.839
It's a cologne.

263
24:20.079 --> 24:21.839
But I don't even wear cologne.

264
24:25.000 --> 24:26.000
Doesn't matter.

265
24:26.759 --> 24:29.160
Anyway, when the time comes,

266
24:29.240 --> 24:29.920
once winter rolls around,

267
24:30.000 --> 24:32.216
I'll take you to Norway to see the snow, and you'll know.

268
24:32.240 --> 24:33.240
Okay.

269
24:35.200 --> 24:36.439
You know,

270
24:36.519 --> 24:39.599
in Norway, the sun doesn't rise until 10 a.m.,

271
24:40.319 --> 24:42.559
and it sets at 1 p.m.

272
24:43.160 --> 24:44.720
There are only three hours of daylight.

273
24:45.759 --> 24:48.080
Why is it so short?

274
24:48.160 --> 24:49.160
I know, right?

275
24:50.160 --> 24:51.840
So when I first got there,

276
24:51.920 --> 24:53.240
I really couldn't get used to it.

277
24:54.079 --> 24:56.119
I always felt like my time was being stolen.

278
24:58.200 --> 24:59.200
Later on,

279
25:00.599 --> 25:02.839
I realized there's plenty to do at night, too.

280
25:04.000 --> 25:07.680
I stopped stressing over having only three hours of daylight.

281
25:10.559 --> 25:12.279
Slowly, I realized

282
25:12.359 --> 25:13.719
the night is actually pretty nice.

283
25:14.839 --> 25:17.519
The darkness brings me peace and calm.

284
25:22.440 --> 25:23.440
Unlike the daytime,

285
25:24.279 --> 25:29.440
when I have to put on a fake persona.

286
25:35.799 --> 25:36.799
Look.

287
25:37.319 --> 25:38.919
The scenery there is truly breathtaking.

288
25:40.519 --> 25:42.160
Too bad. I really regret

289
25:42.759 --> 25:44.799
not taking the cable car up the mountain back then.

290
25:48.279 --> 25:50.200
But if you were there,

291
25:50.799 --> 25:52.039
I probably would've gone on it.

292
26:00.720 --> 26:01.720
Well,

293
26:02.920 --> 26:05.079
I hope I can save up enough money to travel abroad.

294
26:07.400 --> 26:08.400
Look.

295
26:09.400 --> 26:10.479
Such a beautiful

296
26:10.559 --> 26:13.400
postcard from 69 degrees north latitude,

297
26:13.480 --> 26:14.999
and I could only send it to myself.

298
26:15.079 --> 26:16.079
What a shame.

299
26:18.319 --> 26:20.839
Next time, if you're not with me,

300
26:22.799 --> 26:23.799
I think.

301
26:26.640 --> 26:27.640
I'll send one to you.

302
26:31.240 --> 26:34.079
People always say Norway is freezing.

303
26:36.640 --> 26:39.480
But when you actually go there,

304
26:40.640 --> 26:42.000
bundle up in thick clothes,

305
26:43.759 --> 26:45.160
step onto that white snow,

306
26:47.279 --> 26:49.920
and watch your breath turn into white mist,

307
26:52.079 --> 26:53.079
you'll realize

308
26:54.000 --> 26:55.000
that in fact,

309
26:56.680 --> 27:01.039
it's the warmest winter of all.

310
27:04.279 --> 27:05.279
That's why.

311
27:06.279 --> 27:07.640
I wrote that line.

312
27:12.680 --> 27:13.680
Then,

313
27:14.920 --> 27:16.319
give this one to me.

314
27:17.240 --> 27:19.480
Let's pretend the postcard you sent back then

315
27:20.240 --> 27:21.839
has finally reached me now.

316
27:22.359 --> 27:23.359
Okay.

317
27:53.160 --> 27:54.160
Pao Bei.

318
28:17.480 --> 28:18.480
Pao Bei.

319
28:26.599 --> 28:27.599
Pao Bei.

320
28:32.559 --> 28:33.680
Pao Bei.

321
28:48.359 --> 28:49.359
Pao Bei.

322
29:16.799 --> 29:19.279
P'Eng, is that you?

323
29:19.359 --> 29:20.640
Mom?

324
29:20.720 --> 29:21.880
Is that you?

325
29:22.480 --> 29:23.480
P'Eng.

326
29:24.039 --> 29:25.039
It's Mom.

327
29:25.960 --> 29:27.560
I'm right here.

328
29:27.640 --> 29:28.640
Come here.

329
29:37.440 --> 29:38.720
Mom!

330
29:41.480 --> 29:42.480
Mom!

331
29:43.240 --> 29:44.240
How did you...

332
29:44.880 --> 29:46.759
end up like this?

333
29:48.519 --> 29:50.000
You're finally here.

334
29:50.920 --> 29:53.039
Didn't you see the hint I left for you?

335
29:53.880 --> 29:55.640
The picture we painted together.

336
29:55.720 --> 29:57.279
Didn't you find it?

337
29:58.359 --> 30:00.200
That painting...

338
30:00.720 --> 30:03.440
So you were the one who buried it?

339
30:06.920 --> 30:08.039
Don't take my child away!

340
30:08.839 --> 30:09.360
No!

341
30:09.440 --> 30:09.679
Come here!

342
30:09.759 --> 30:10.640
No!

343
30:10.720 --> 30:11.080
Mom!

344
30:11.160 --> 30:11.600
Stop!

345
30:11.680 --> 30:12.039
Mom!

346
30:12.119 --> 30:12.800
No!

347
30:12.880 --> 30:14.039
Don't take my child away!

348
32:02.119 --> 32:03.519
Good morning, Mr. Pao Bei.

349
32:06.519 --> 32:07.400
Good morning.

350
32:07.480 --> 32:08.719
Did you sleep well?

351
32:08.799 --> 32:11.136
As Master P'Eng instructed, the kids have been dropped off at school.

352
32:11.160 --> 32:12.039
Now that you're awake,

353
32:12.119 --> 32:13.959
you may head to the dining room for breakfast.

354
32:14.559 --> 32:16.000
I slept pretty well.

355
32:18.480 --> 32:19.039
Where...

356
32:19.119 --> 32:20.279
Where is he?

357
32:20.359 --> 32:22.439
Master P'Eng was in the kitchen bright and early,

358
32:22.519 --> 32:24.439
making breakfast with Mr. A Pong.

359
32:24.519 --> 32:26.519
He's just waiting for you to wake up and enjoy it.

360
32:26.960 --> 32:28.160
He made breakfast himself?

361
32:36.160 --> 32:36.959
What's this?

362
32:37.039 --> 32:38.279
Master P'Eng had this prepared.

363
32:38.319 --> 32:39.599
It's your outfit for today.

364
32:40.880 --> 32:42.880
Why do I have to dress so formally?

365
32:42.960 --> 32:44.680
Are we going to some kind of event?

366
32:45.839 --> 32:46.999
I wouldn't know about that.

367
32:47.079 --> 32:49.640
But I'm sure you'll look dashing in it.

368
32:50.519 --> 32:52.320
Once you've washed up and gotten dressed,

369
32:52.400 --> 32:53.719
you can head downstairs.

370
32:53.799 --> 32:55.559
We'll be waiting for you in the dining room.

371
33:06.720 --> 33:09.160
What on earth is this guy up to?

372
33:15.920 --> 33:16.920
Good morning.

373
33:18.920 --> 33:19.920
Whoa.

374
33:20.839 --> 33:22.800
Another huge breakfast spread today.

375
33:22.880 --> 33:24.120
Did you cook this yourself?

376
33:24.200 --> 33:25.600
Yep.

377
33:25.680 --> 33:26.560
I made all of this.

378
33:26.640 --> 33:27.400
What do you think?

379
33:27.480 --> 33:28.920
Come on, you made it?

380
33:29.000 --> 33:30.216
All you did was toss the ingredients

381
33:30.240 --> 33:31.616
I chopped and seasoned into the pan.

382
33:31.640 --> 33:35.799
A joint effort between Tailan's most handsome boss and its finest chef.

383
33:38.480 --> 33:39.320
Where is he?

384
33:39.400 --> 33:40.080
Is he up yet?

385
33:40.160 --> 33:42.200
Mr. Pao Bei should be down any minute.

386
34:13.480 --> 34:14.720
Are you...

387
34:14.800 --> 34:17.479
heading to a fashion gala or something?

388
34:17.559 --> 34:19.720
Dressed to the nines first thing in the morning.

389
34:19.800 --> 34:21.439
You're so weird.

390
34:21.519 --> 34:22.960
Go ask him about it.

391
34:27.239 --> 34:29.999
Look at you, so dashing and debonair.

392
34:30.079 --> 34:32.719
Dressed like that, everyone can tell you're mine.

393
34:33.320 --> 34:34.999
Yours?

394
34:35.079 --> 34:36.720
Of course he's Boss P'Eng's.

395
34:36.800 --> 34:38.599
Everyone here works for Boss P'Eng.

396
34:38.679 --> 34:39.679
Isn't that right?

397
34:40.280 --> 34:41.640
Aren't you one of his people, too?

398
34:42.400 --> 34:44.320
He agreed to be my assistant last night.

399
34:44.400 --> 34:45.959
So, technically,

400
34:46.039 --> 34:47.839
you're part of Boss P'Eng's company now, too.

401
34:48.800 --> 34:49.840
Just eat your congee.

402
34:51.320 --> 34:53.079
I made all of this specially for you.

403
34:53.159 --> 34:54.159
Mhm.

404
34:55.760 --> 34:57.280
Why don't I get this kind of service?

405
34:57.880 --> 34:59.360
You want service like this?

406
35:00.960 --> 35:04.639
Then take good care of me and your boss from now on.

407
35:06.280 --> 35:07.480
As if I care.

408
35:08.360 --> 35:09.479
Stop piling up my plate.

409
35:09.559 --> 35:10.760
I can't finish all of this.

410
35:12.000 --> 35:13.000
Well,

411
35:14.039 --> 35:15.135
eat this shumai first, then.

412
35:15.159 --> 35:16.159
It's really good.

413
35:22.159 --> 35:23.159
Is it good?

414
35:26.239 --> 35:27.239
Delicious.

415
35:43.400 --> 35:44.760
Master, slow down.

416
35:44.840 --> 35:46.936
Keep eating like that and I'll lose track of your calories.

417
35:46.960 --> 35:48.000
Don't bother counting.

418
35:48.840 --> 35:51.360
I got a massive workout last night.

419
35:54.119 --> 35:55.400
I need to eat up.

420
36:06.360 --> 36:07.880
You guys don't need to wait on me.

421
36:08.519 --> 36:09.840
I can manage on my own.

422
36:10.679 --> 36:12.039
Have you had breakfast yet?

423
36:12.119 --> 36:14.039
We only eat after the masters have finished.

424
36:14.119 --> 36:15.119
Those are the rules.

425
36:16.159 --> 36:19.119
There's way too much food here for us to finish.

426
36:19.199 --> 36:20.319
It'd be a shame to waste it.

427
36:20.880 --> 36:22.080
Come sit down and eat with us.

428
36:23.039 --> 36:25.800
We're not allowed to dine at the same table as the masters.

429
36:29.960 --> 36:31.800
Who made the rule that they can't eat with us?

430
36:33.159 --> 36:34.159
Beats me.

431
36:34.719 --> 36:36.719
Probably a tradition passed down by our ancestors.

432
36:37.559 --> 36:38.079
Don't worry about it.

433
36:38.159 --> 36:38.959
Just eat your food.

434
36:39.039 --> 36:39.760
Go on, eat.

435
36:39.840 --> 36:40.639
Mhm.

436
36:40.719 --> 36:42.159
They're all still on empty stomachs,

437
36:42.719 --> 36:43.639
just standing there watching me eat.

438
36:43.719 --> 36:45.199
I can't take a single bite like this.

439
36:54.119 --> 36:54.440
Fine.

440
36:54.960 --> 36:56.639
I'll make a special exception today.

441
36:56.719 --> 36:57.719
I'm in a good mood.

442
36:58.480 --> 36:59.400
Everyone, sit down

443
36:59.480 --> 37:00.119
and eat together.

444
37:00.199 --> 37:01.280
No leftovers allowed.

445
37:01.360 --> 37:02.479
Got that?

446
37:02.559 --> 37:03.559
Yes.

447
37:06.159 --> 37:06.599
Go on.

448
37:06.679 --> 37:07.679
Take a seat over there.

449
37:16.400 --> 37:17.840
Now this is a first.

450
37:17.920 --> 37:19.559
They actually get to eat my cooking.

451
37:21.000 --> 37:22.000
Ever since you showed up,

452
37:22.079 --> 37:24.039
unusual things have been happening more and more.

453
37:28.079 --> 37:29.079
This is good.

454
38:14.960 --> 38:15.999
Mingkun.

455
38:16.079 --> 38:18.135
These clothes are too hot and get in the way of my work.

456
38:18.159 --> 38:20.039
I should just change back into my own clothes.

457
38:20.119 --> 38:22.559
I'm afraid you'll have to run that by the Master first.

458
38:23.559 --> 38:25.359
I'm just more used to how things were before.

459
38:25.760 --> 38:27.439
Why is he suddenly acting like this?

460
38:27.519 --> 38:28.679
I'm not used to it at all.

461
38:29.400 --> 38:30.535
These are the Master's orders.

462
38:30.559 --> 38:32.400
Their sole job is to assist you.

463
38:35.000 --> 38:36.519
How did it come to this?

464
38:37.239 --> 38:39.280
Because you belong to the Master now.

465
38:41.360 --> 38:42.840
Since when do I belong to him?

466
38:45.280 --> 38:46.720
After what happened last night,

467
38:46.800 --> 38:49.000
don't tell me you're going to pretend nothing happened?

468
38:57.519 --> 38:58.519
What happened?

469
38:59.960 --> 39:01.240
It's just a little prick.

470
39:01.320 --> 39:02.200
Ambulance!

471
39:02.280 --> 39:02.920
Call an ambulance!

472
39:03.000 --> 39:03.639
Hurry!

473
39:03.719 --> 39:04.599
Hey, come back!

474
39:04.679 --> 39:05.519
It's just a tiny cut.

475
39:05.599 --> 39:06.880
It's no big deal.

476
39:06.960 --> 39:07.599
Master,

477
39:07.679 --> 39:09.439
just put this band-aid on and it'll be fine.

478
39:11.199 --> 39:12.440
I'm fine, really.

479
39:12.960 --> 39:14.720
If you keep overreacting like this,

480
39:14.800 --> 39:16.959
I'm seriously going to start ignoring you.

481
39:17.039 --> 39:17.920
This one is waterproof.

482
39:18.000 --> 39:19.320
You can keep it on in the shower.

483
39:24.719 --> 39:25.360
Master P'Eng,

484
39:25.440 --> 39:26.280
Mr. Pao Bei.

485
39:26.360 --> 39:28.240
I have some things to attend to over there,

486
39:28.320 --> 39:29.920
so I'll go take care of them now.

487
39:30.000 --> 39:31.000
Mhm.

488
39:32.039 --> 39:32.800
How is it?

489
39:32.880 --> 39:33.880
Does it still hurt?

490
39:35.159 --> 39:36.800
Oh, so now you care if I'm in pain?

491
39:36.880 --> 39:38.680
When I was crying out in pain last night...

492
39:38.760 --> 39:39.800
"It hurts, it hurts!"

493
39:39.880 --> 39:41.600
Why were you enjoying it so much back then?

494
39:42.440 --> 39:45.400
Isn't that why I made you breakfast first thing this morning

495
39:45.480 --> 39:46.560
and had people wait on you?

496
39:47.199 --> 39:47.680
What's wrong?

497
39:47.760 --> 39:48.800
Not satisfied?

498
39:50.400 --> 39:51.959
I'd rather you didn't do any of this.

499
39:52.039 --> 39:53.575
Having all these people hovering around me...

500
39:53.599 --> 39:54.760
I'm not used to it.

501
39:54.840 --> 39:58.000
What's the big deal? You'll learn to get used to it.

502
39:56.440 --> 39:57.800
You'll get used to it soon enough.

503
40:03.199 --> 40:04.519
After all,

504
40:04.599 --> 40:05.800
since you're mine,

505
40:05.880 --> 40:07.495
you'll need to start keeping pace with me.

506
40:07.519 --> 40:08.519
Got it?

507
40:09.280 --> 40:10.360
Me?

508
40:10.440 --> 40:11.920
Since when am I yours?

509
40:13.000 --> 40:14.159
What do you mean?

510
40:17.000 --> 40:18.119
I mean, I...

511
40:18.199 --> 40:21.239
Aren't you mine now?

512
40:23.760 --> 40:25.320
I mean, I'm my own person.

513
40:25.400 --> 40:26.880
I don't belong to anyone.

514
40:29.079 --> 40:30.159
Then last night...

515
40:31.119 --> 40:32.239
What was that?

516
40:35.079 --> 40:38.199
Just two consenting adults blowing off some steam.

517
40:41.039 --> 40:42.440
Are you playing me again?

518
40:43.320 --> 40:44.959
I was just joking with you.

519
40:45.039 --> 40:46.639
Why are you getting so worked up?

520
40:46.719 --> 40:48.559
Are you freaking playing me again?!

521
40:48.639 --> 40:49.679
Why are you yelling again?

522
40:49.719 --> 40:51.359
Can't we just talk like civilized people?

523
40:53.039 --> 40:54.240
It's fine, A Pong.

524
40:54.320 --> 40:55.599
We're just messing around.

525
40:55.679 --> 40:57.095
Who the hell is messing around with you?!

526
40:57.119 --> 40:59.015
I told you to talk nicely and watch your damn mouth!

527
40:59.039 --> 40:59.800
Are you deaf?!

528
40:59.880 --> 41:00.559
What's it to you?

529
41:00.639 --> 41:01.760
Get lost!

530
41:01.840 --> 41:02.720
Boss P'Eng,

531
41:02.800 --> 41:04.615
let's just talk it out. We're all on the same side here.

532
41:04.639 --> 41:06.519
You're going to scare Pao Bei acting like this.

533
41:07.599 --> 41:09.360
I'm asking you one last time.

534
41:10.920 --> 41:12.159
Last night...

535
41:13.599 --> 41:14.959
What the hell was that between us?

536
41:17.840 --> 41:19.559
What did you two do last night?

537
41:22.760 --> 41:23.959
Him and me...

538
41:24.039 --> 41:25.039
The two of us...

539
41:26.719 --> 41:27.800
slept together.

540
41:27.880 --> 41:28.920
What?

541
41:30.280 --> 41:31.800
You... What did you just say?

542
41:31.880 --> 41:32.920
Are you deaf?

543
41:33.000 --> 41:34.495
I said we slept together. We hooked up.

544
41:34.519 --> 41:35.519
Get it now?

545
41:38.679 --> 41:39.679
P'Eng!

546
41:41.960 --> 41:43.239
Don't be rude to our guest.
